<h1>Grade scales & conversion</h1>

<p>Climbing has no single global grading system — Boulder and Sport
climbing each have several scales in real use, and which one you'll see
depends on where a route or problem was set. This page shows how every
scale this app supports lines up against the others, and where each
equivalence actually comes from.</p>

<h2>How to read the tables</h2>

<p>Each row is one real difficulty step. Read across a row to see how
that step is expressed in every other scale this app supports. A blank
cell (—) means that scale doesn't have a distinct step at that
difficulty — it's coarser than the reference scale the row is built
from, not missing data.</p>

<p>Grades you enter or see anywhere else in this app always resolve
through this same conversion data — there's no separate, hand-kept
table anywhere that could drift out of sync with what's shown here.</p>

